<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Malaka</h1><p class="st-meta">770 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.) · capital Malaka</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Phoenician harbour on the Costa del Sol that grew into Málaga, one of Iberia's oldest cities.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> settled the bay of Málaga in the 8th century BCE, first at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerro-del-villar">Cerro del Villar</a> on an island in the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalhorce">Guadalhorce</a>, and then on the hill below the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcazaba-of-malaga">Alcazaba</a>, where Malaka grew into the main settlement by the 6th century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Malaka traded with the Iberian peoples of the interior and lived from fishing, fish salting and crafts. It was later drawn into the Carthaginian sphere, and its coins with Punic legends showed a smith god with tongs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> described it as a market for the nomads of the opposite African coast.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 206 BCE Malaka came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as an allied city. As Malaca it received municipal status under the Flavian emperors, recorded in the bronze <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lex-flavia-malacitana">Lex Flavia Malacitana</a>, and continued as a major port of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-baetica">Hispania Baetica</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 770 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:44.38%;width:11.22%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>770 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Malaka</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Phoenician religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Phoenician</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Malaca, Malaga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-488&amp;focus=malaka" aria-label="Malaka on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4574 758 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Malaka lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5259 1106h0M4881 1072h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4894 1014h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4894 1014h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-488&amp;focus=malaka">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
